edicated%20servers]Compatibility[/url] | [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/220#:~:text=If%20something%20doesn%27t%20work%2C%20please%20post%20these%20files]Troubleshooting[/url] | [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/220#:~:text=the%20World%20Map%20now%20lies%20on%20a%20painted]Changelog[/url][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Every marker on the world map[/b]: spires, altars, sanctums, vaults, lairs, towns, camps, mines, caves, garrisons, quests, lore rumors, graves, and all 448 gold, 1032 silver and 1562 wooden chests, and the Hollow Halls' 66 end-room sarcophagi.
[*][b]Mining, Materials, Plants, Bait, Trees and Ground[/b]: every ore deposit, material, plant patch and bait spot, read from the game's own world files, and heat maps of every forest and of the rock and sand recipes ask for.
[*][b]Creatures[/b]: where every creature spawns, 136 kinds, from the animals you can tame to the Fell, Scavengers and Ancient Constructs.
[*][b]Lore Notes and Bosses[/b]: every note and diary and every boss, with the ones you've read or beaten grayed out or hidden. Return Beacons and every well and water barrel too.
[*][b]Unique gear, collectibles and cosmetics[/b]: every unique weapon, ring and piece of gear, the journal's collectibles (fossils, paintings, mosaic pieces...), every cosmetic set piece placed in the world, Fell Summoning Stones and each region's night plants.
[*][b]Hollow Halls[/b]: inside a hall the World Map shows that hall alone, seen from above in the game's own textures, with its Return Beacons numbered in order, and footprints on the minimap show where you've been.
[*][b]Ancient Vaults and Spires[/b]: the same maps, a floor at a time, with live traps, doors that show locked or open, and where each teleport pad takes you.
[*][b]Level Areas[/b]: the world map in the areas of the enemies' levels, from 1 at the start to 48 in the north, each with its level, read from the game's own data.
[*][b]Regions[/b]: show only the regions you pick (the rest dimmed or hidden) with their borders drawn.
[*][b]G G: what's nearby glows[/b]: press G twice and the chests, notes and bosses near you glow through walls and floors, and the ore you track is outlined on screen.
[*][b]A Map Key & Filters panel[/b] built from the game's own UI art: an icon, a count and an ON/OFF switch for every marker type, whole categories at a click, filters for your custom pins, and padlocks that keep a filter as you set it.
[*][b]A Map Desk[/b]: the World Map on a painted cartographer's desk with a lantern and a 3D compass that swings as you drag the map.
[*][b]Two more zoom steps out[/b] on the world map, and [b]Page Up / Page Down[/b] (or numpad + and -) to zoom a step at a time.
[*][b]Find on the map[/b]: press [b]Shift+F[/b], type a name or a kind of place, and the map moves to show it.
[*][b]Fog and pin modes[/b]: the game's own fog, a light fog over a fully drawn map, or no fog; and pins only where you've been, grayed out in unexplored land, or all of them.
[*][b]Looted chests[/b]: open a chest and it's hidden or grayed out with a check mark until it refills, and it keeps the check mark after. Shared with other players who have the mod.
[*][b]A minimap on your HUD[/b] with the map's terrain, the time of day or the weather, and other players, that you can move, resize and zoom.
[*][b]All 15 game languages[/b]: the mod's text follows the game's language.
[*][b]Client only[/b]: works in single player, hosted games and on any dedicated server. Nothing goes on the server, and other players don't need it.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1793549371-1789962003.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Map Desk[/b][/size]

The World Map lies on a painted cartographer's desk that pans and zooms with it: a gold frame, a lantern with a soft blue glow, a 3D compass that holds north and swings when you drag the map, scrolls, a dish of map pins and two survivor notes written in the game's language. With it on, panning stops at the map's edges at every zoom. [b]Settings > Look > Map Desk[/b] turns it off; it starts on only with the game's Ultra graphics preset.

[line]

[size=4][b]The Map Key & Filters panel[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845210-913068383.jpg[/img][/center]

[list]
[*][b]Every gold and silver chest in the world is included[/b]: all 448 gold chests and 1032 silver chests have their own rows in the filter, so you can show just the chests you're hunting. [b]Wooden Chest[/b] (World & Resources, off at first) adds the world's 1562 wooden chests, wooden sarcophagi and locked wooden chests.
[*]Click a row to show or hide that marker type.
[*][b]SHOW ALL / HIDE ALL[/b] at the top switch every marker type at once.
[*][b]Search this list[/b], under them: type part of a row's name and only the matching rows show, their sections opened (folded or locked ones too). [b]Esc[/b] or the x clears it. From 3 letters it also finds places by their name (a lore note, a boss, a place, a pin): the row they're in shows with that name after it, even when the row is off. Find (Shift+F) takes you there.
[*][b]REGIONS[/b], under them (with Settings > Filters > Region Filter on): a row per region in level order (Springlands, Revelwood, Blackmire, Nomad Highlands, Kindlewastes, Albaneve Summits, Veilwater Basin, Cinder's Cradle), each with its own ON / OFF, in a drawer [b]+ / -[/b] folds away. Click the row's name to switch them all on or all off; [b]Ctrl + click[/b] a region to show only that one. Pins outside the regions that are on are dimmed ([b]DIM[/b]) or not shown at all ([b]HIDE[/b]), and their borders are drawn as a dotted gold line. Quest pins, lore rumors and your own pins always show. Requested by VintageMarble and FrostyBou.
[*]Click a category header to switch the whole category; [b]+ / -[/b] folds it, and it stays folded the next time you play. [b]Drag a category header[/b] up or down to move the category; the order is remembered.
[*]The rows in each category are sorted by name in your language.
[*]The mouse wheel or the scroll bar scrolls the list.
[*][b]Click one of the mod's own icons[/b] (a collectible, an ore, a Wooden Chest) for Send Ping and Set as Waypoint. Press on a pin and drag to pan the map.
[*][b]Mark a place done[/b]: [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] a town, camp, sanctum, vault or other place for a check mark; again clears it. Marked places follow Completed Places in Settings.
[*][b]Hide a marker's row from the map[/b]: [b]Alt + left click[/b] the marker, or [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] one that can't be marked. [b]Ctrl+Z[/b] undoes a filter change and [b]Ctrl+Y[/b] redoes it. A message names the filter and ON or OFF.
[*][b]Rebind anything[/b]: [Keys] in minimap_config.ini holds every key and controller button.
[*][b]Filter presets[/b]: the [b]1 2 3 4 5[/b] buttons under Show All / Hide All. Click one to apply it, [b]Ctrl + click[/b] (or [b]Ctrl+Alt+1[/b] to [b]Ctrl+Alt+5[/b]) to save your current filters and map settings into it (fog, pins, marker size, looted and completed places, regions, level areas), right click to rename it. [b]Alt+1[/b] to [b]Alt+5[/b] apply them from the map; on a controller [b]LT + Left/Right[/b] steps through them. They start as Chests, Mining, Exploring, Bosses and Plants.
[*][b]CUSTOM PINS[/b]: click a pin icon to show or hide your own pins of that kind.
[*][b]Tab[/b] (or the - button at the top) folds the panel away; to use another key, set [i]PanelToggle=[/i] under [i][Keys][/i] in [i]minimap_config.ini[/i] (a letter, a digit, F1 to F12, CapsLock, Home, End... or None). [i]Glow=[/i] there sets G G's key, and [i]MinimapMouse=[/i] the keys held for the minimap's mouse (Shift+Alt at first; up to three of Shift, Ctrl, Alt and a key, joined with +). The [b]cog[/b] opens Settings.
[*][b]With a controller[/b]: [b]View[/b] on the World Map moves it into the panel; the D-pad steps between rows and buttons, [b]A[/b] clicks, [b]B[/b] goes back to the map. On the map itself, with [b]RS[/b] (the right stick pressed in) held: [b]D-pad Up[/b] marks what is at the middle of the view, [b]Down[/b] hides its row, [b]Left[/b] and [b]Right[/b] undo and redo.
[*][b]Filter locks[/b]: the padlock left of a switch locks that filter. A locked filter keeps its ON or OFF through SHOW ALL / HIDE ALL, reloads and updates, and a locked category also stays open or closed; you can still click it. [b]Hold[/b] SHOW ALL or HIDE ALL to change locked filters too.
[*][b]Lore Notes[/b] (Quests & Rumors): every note and diary in the world, 574. Notes you've read are grayed out or hidden, like looted chests; unread ones are drawn bigger on an amber ring so they stand out. Hover one for its title. [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] one to mark it read (or not read) by hand, saved per character.
[*][b]Unique Weapons[/b] and [b]Unique Equipment[/b] (World & Resources): the one-of-a-kind weapons (40, like the Wailing Blade and Talion's Bow) and rings and gear (16, like the Gemini Ring and the Flaming Gauntlets), each at the chest or place it is in, with its own icon and name. It counts as found once you've picked it up, however you got it (an enemy's drop, a loot mod), or its gold or silver chest is looted; [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] one to mark it found by hand, saved per character. [b]Find[/b] finds them by name. Requested by Gadn.
[*][b]Collectibles[/b] (World & Resources): the journal's collectibles, 133, lying in the world or in a chest: fossils, skeleton pieces, the bard's paintings, Drak reliefs, mosaic and map pieces, meteorites and more, each with its own icon and name. Found once you've picked it up (or its chest is looted); [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] one to mark it found by hand, saved per character. [b]Find[/b] finds them by name.
[*][b]Cosmetics[/b] (World & Resources): the cosmetic set pieces placed in the world, 115: Efflorescent Hope, Mothling, Royal, Winterly, Hollow's Eve and the other sets, each piece with its own icon and name. Found once you've picked it up (or its chest is looted); [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] one to mark it found by hand, saved per character.
[*][b]Fell Summoning Stones[/b] (World & Resources): the 45 stones where Shroud Spores conjure a Fell enemy, one tier per region.
[*][b]Bosses[/b] (World & Resources): the world's bosses, named like their health bar. A boss you've beaten gets a check mark for good, and is grayed out or hidden only while it's dead, until it comes back by the same rule as a looted chest. A boss you kill is seen dying when you're there, so beating one again grays it too. The game keeps no record of beating some of them, and the mod can't see the Fell Critter Queens and the Fog Predator: [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] a boss on the map to step it: beaten (grayed), came back (check mark only), never beaten. Beaten marks are saved per character, the timers per world.
[*][b]Return Beacons[/b] (Shroud & Vaults): all 282.
[*][b]Water Source[/b] (World & Resources) also shows the world's wells and water barrels you can drink from, and the ones you build.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792934139-1121249783.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845219-1053091644.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]G G: what's nearby glows[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792934139-1608303195.jpg[/img][/center]

Press [b]G[/b] twice quickly while playing. For 14 seconds everything within 75 m that isn't done yet glows through walls and floors: unlooted gold, silver and wooden chests, unread lore notes, bosses you haven't beaten, and what the quests you're on want there (the quest's item or place, with its quest icon), while their filters are on. They pulse on the world map and the minimap too, so you can see which way to go.

On the minimap, the ones 4 m or more above or below you get a green up or orange down caret, so you know whether to go up or down.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792873369-183261406.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1793455259-2005735288.jpg[/img][/center]

[b]Vein sight[/b]: the ore and materials of the Mining and Materials rows you have on show for 30 seconds too, for the deposits the map shows near you. Out to 50 m each vein is outlined on screen in its ore's colour, with the deposit's icon in its middle. Within 10 m of where you pressed it, the ore of the Mining rows you have on also shows through the rock for 5 seconds, as see-through shaded surfaces in its ore's colour.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1793758507-885087891.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1793758507-1571212113.jpg[/img][/center] On the minimap a deposit 4 m or more above or below you gets the same caret, so you know whether to dig up or down.

[line]

[size=4][b]Mining, Materials, Plants, Bait, Trees and Ground[/b][/size]


Read from the game's own world files, so every spot is where the game put it. Each kind has its own row in the Map Key (all off at first), and hovering an icon on the world map names it.
[list]
[*][b]MINING[/b]: every ore deposit, 21 kinds (copper, iron, silver, gold, sulfur, salt...), 7,452 in all.
[*][b]MATERIALS[/b]: farm soil, fertilised farm soil, flower soil, twigs, bones, tar, toxic slime, luminous growth, ice, gold coins, archaic essence.
[*][b]PLANTS[/b]: 30 harvestable plants plus Date and Yucca Fruit, as patches, and each region's night plants (Midnight Lily, Gloomberry, Calla Luna, Shadowbloom, Glimmer Gentian, Stapelia Starflower, Passionflower, Gleam Root) where they grow at night.
[*][b]BAIT[/b]: fireflies, moths, grasshoppers, pillbugs, frogs and more.
[*][b]TREES[/b]: each forest as a heat map in its tree type's colour, as thick as its trees grow, 18 types; the big ones carry their name.
[*][b]GROUND[/b]: the rock and sand recipes ask for (Granite, Basalt, Cinder Rock, Shell Limestone, Sandstone, Revelwood Stone, Blackmire Stone, Fine Sand, Sand, Veilwater Basin Sand, Cinder's Cradle Sand, Moss) as heat maps where they make up the ground.
[*][b]Roads[/b] and [b]Surface Water[/b] (under GROUND): every road on the island, and its lakes, rivers and pools as the world starts out, on the World Map and the minimap.
[/list]
Deposits, materials, plants and bait also show on the minimap and in Find.

[size=4][b]Creatures[/b][/size]

Where every creature spawns, read from the game's world files: 136 kinds, from the animals you can tame (Flightless Redtail, Common Goat, Fae Deer, Yak...) and the wildlife to the Fell, Scavengers, Vukah, Drak'Dal, the Hollow and the Ancient Constructs. Each has its own row in the CREATURES category, all off at first, with the game's own names; type a name in the Map Key's search to find it. Spawn points close together make one marker. Creatures also show on the minimap. Bosses keep their own Boss row.

[b]Nearby Creatures Only[/b] (Settings > Minimap) shows the live creatures within 75 m on the minimap instead of their spawn points, each with a height arrow, and a ring while an enemy fights you (red) or searches for you (amber). [b]G G[/b] then outlines them through walls in those colours. [b]Hide on World Map[/b], under it, keeps their spawn points off the World Map too, except the creatures Find is looking for.

[size=4][b]Level Areas[/b][/size]

[b]Settings > World Map > Level Areas[/b] shows the world map in the areas of the enemies' levels, from 1 where you start to 48 in the Albaneve Summits: each area tinted by its level, with the borders between them and its level in a badge. Read from the levels the game gives its spawners, loot and props. [b]Tint Strength[/b], under it, sets how strongly the colours cover the map (10% to 80%); the borders and badges stay as they are.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1793454871-1870413585.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Find (Shift+F)[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792776528-804463773.jpg[/img][/center]

On the world map, press [b]Shift+F[/b] or click [b]FIND[/b]. Type a name or a kind of place, for example [i]gold[/i], [i]spire[/i] or [i]garrison[/i]. Every match is listed with its region, its distance from you, and [i][Locked][/i] if you haven't unlocked it yet.
[list]
[*]Click a result twice, double-click it or press [b]Enter[/b], and the map moves to show it.
[*][b]All Matching Places - Zoom to fit[/b] shows every match at once.
[*]Words in any order: [i]chest gold[/i] finds the Gold Chests. Names holding the whole text come first, then every word, then only some of them. [b]Enter[/b] with nothing selected shows the best matches.
[*][b]Exact match[/b] ([b]Ctrl+E[/b] or the controller's Y) keeps only names holding the whole text.
[*][b]F2[/b] (or [b]Ctrl+F[/b]) switches whether Find skips marker types you've hidden with the filters. Pick a result a filter hides and the Map Key opens its row and flashes it.
[*]Lore notes and bosses are found by their own names.
[*]Items the game always puts in one chest or container are found by their names too: type [i]ghost glider[/i] and the result is the chest it's in; picking it turns on that chest's row. Random chest loot isn't known ahead.
[*]The mouse wheel or the scroll bar scrolls a long list of results.
[*][b]Esc[/b] closes it (Shift+F types a capital F in the search).
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792777201-1180845193.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1793549371-1789962003.jpg[/img][/center]

The [b]cog[/b] on the Map Key (and the one under the minimap) opens Settings, and so does [b]Alt+Shift+M[/b] (LB + D-pad Down on a controller), while you play too:
[list]
[*][b]FOG:[/b] [b]EXPLORED[/b] is the game's own fog, [b]HYBRID[/b] draws the whole map with unexplored land under a light fog, [b]REVEAL ALL[/b] has no fog.
[*][b]PINS:[/b] [b]EXPLORED[/b] shows pins only where you've been, [b]HYBRID[/b] grays out pins in unexplored land, [b]REVEAL ALL[/b] shows every pin. EXPLORED also keeps everything the game itself shows in land still fogged: places it knows of, places you've discovered, and lore rumor hints. With EXPLORED and HYBRID, a place you haven't discovered yet (the game would hide it) is grayed out, even where the fog is cleared; REVEAL ALL shows it in full colour.
[*][b]World Map[/b]: [b]Custom Marker Size[/b] (your own pins); [b]Looted / Read / Beaten[/b] (hide looted chests, read lore notes and beaten bosses, or gray them out with a check mark); [b]Completed Places[/b] (show or hide the places the game marks done, like cleared roots, used obelisks and cleared vaults, the Flame and Night Sanctums you've visited and the places you've marked done with Ctrl + click); [b]Region Names[/b] (on at first: each region's name as a faint watermark, in the game's language); [b]Stacked Pins List[/b] (off at first: rest the cursor on pins on top of each other and a card lists them all, a click on a row opens its menu); [b]Level Areas[/b] (off at first: the world map in the areas of the enemies' levels, tinted from green through orange and red to purple and blue, with the borders and each area's level in a badge) and [b]Tint Strength[/b] under it.
[*][b]Minimap[/b]: [b]Show Minimap[/b], [b]Minimap Info Bar[/b] (off hides the bar under the minimap; the cog moves to the map's bottom-left corner), [b]Minimap Terrain[/b], [b]Minimap Rotation[/b] (North Up, or Facing Up: the minimap turns with your character), [b]Minimap Border[/b] (ORNATE or THIN), [b]Minimap Icon[/b] (sun/moon or weather), [b]Time Format[/b] (1:00 PM or 13:00), [b]Position (X, Y, Z)[/b] (off at first: your position under the minimap and the X and Z under the cursor on the world map, with a copy button; requested by Loling91), and [b]Nearby Creatures Only[/b] (off at first: the minimap shows the live creatures within 75 m instead of their spawn points; see Creatures) with [b]Hide on World Map[/b] under it.
[*][b]Look[/b]: [b]Map Desk[/b] (see Map Desk), [b]Dungeon Maps[/b] (on at first: the Hollow Hall, vault and spire maps; off, the map opens on the hall's entrance), [b]Vanilla World Map[/b] (off at first: the world map exactly as the game draws it, as your friends without the mod see it; the minimap stays, and its cog is then the way to Settings; requested by menelothar) and [b]Vanilla Minimap[/b] under it (the minimap with the game's own markers only).
[*][b]Filters[/b]: [b]Region Filter[/b] (off at first: the Map Key's REGIONS row) and [b]Filter Locks[/b] (how many filters are locked; Remove All unlocks them).
[/list]
Everything is remembered.

[line]

[size=4][b]Looted chests[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845223-927762810.jpg[/img][/center]

Open a gold or silver chest and the mod marks it looted: hidden, or grayed out with a check mark. Once it refills it's drawn as usual again but keeps its check mark, so you can see which chests you've looted at least once. On the world map, [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] a chest to step it: looted, refilled (check mark only), never looted. Chests you opened before installing the mod aren't known to it: they show until you open them again or Ctrl + left click them. Players who have the mod share them: open a chest and it's marked on their maps too.

Chests refill by the game's own rule: the world is cut into 256 m squares, and 30 minutes after every player has left a square's range (258 m from each of its corners) the game resets it, so its chests refill and its bosses come back. Chests in a Flame Altar's build zone never come back. On a dedicated server the time you're away counts too, if the server's clock kept running (one that stands still while nobody is on counts nothing). Looted chests are saved per world.

If you open chests with another key than E, set [i]InteractKey=[/i] under [i][Chests][/i] in [i]minimap_config.ini[/i]; [i]RespawnMinutes=[/i] and [i]ResetRadius=[/i] (a distance that also holds the timer, 0 at first) are there too.

[line]

[size=4][b]Minimap[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845219-19805001.jpg[/img][/center]

A minimap on your HUD with the World Map's terrain, a compass, the time of day (or the weather) and its zoom level, placed under the Journal [J] tab at first. Cleared places and looted chests show a check mark. A mining or materials deposit within 75 m that is 4 m or more above or below you gets a green up or orange down caret. Your waypoint shows on it, and at its edge pointing the way when it's further off.

[b]Hold Shift + Alt[/b] to set it up. The mouse cursor appears and the camera stops turning, so you won't swing your view or attack. While you hold them:
[list]
[*][b]Drag the minimap[/b] to move it anywhere on screen.
[*][b]Drag its bottom-right corner[/b] to make it bigger or smaller.
[*][b]Mouse wheel[/b] zooms.
[*][b]Double-click the star at the top[/b] to put it back in its default place.
[/list]
Zoom any time with [b][[/b] and [b]][/b] (or numpad - and +), or with the - / + buttons under the minimap; the [b]cog[/b] next to them opens Settings. A gold or silver chest, lore note or boss within 75 m that is 4 m or more above or below you gets a small green up or orange down caret, and so do another player and a player grave (on the world map too). [b]Other Players[/b] in the panel shows other players on the map, and on the minimap as colored arrows that point where they're heading; each player has the same colour on every screen (the first player in the server yellow, the second blue, then red, green, purple and on). With the Town Portal mod, [b]Town Portals[/b] (Fast Travel & Altars) shows its open portals on the map and the minimap in their owner's colour. Position, size and zoom are saved for next time.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845215-1387636545.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845223-993348796.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]Hollow Halls[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1793483538-1836533140.jpg[/img][/center]

Inside a Hollow Hall the [b]World Map[/b] shows that hall alone in a frame of its own, seen from above in the game's own textures: the floor you're on bright, the hall's other levels dimmed, so they never mix. It opens with the whole hall in view and zooms in close. Its [b]Return Beacons[/b] are numbered in the order you reach them, and its chests, lore notes and players show as on the rest of the map (the end room's chests are [b]Dungeon Spoils[/b]: hover one for its name and the Ectoplasm it takes to open). [b]Overworld Map[/b] at the top switches to the world, centred on the hall's entrance, and back; [b]C[/b] centres the hall on you.

The dungeon's name shows at the top, and [b]Ctrl+D[/b] (LB + D-pad Up) switches to the overworld map and back. On an Ancient Spire's top, where its teleport lands you, the maps show the overworld.

[b]Ancient Vaults and Spires[/b] get the same maps, a floor at a time: teleporters split them into floors, and [b]- Floor n / m +[/b] on the map (or [b]Ctrl+Up/Down[/b]) picks one. Traps show live (fireballs and sparks moving, spikes glowing as they come out, plates their switch turned off), doors show locked, closed or open, and hovering a teleport pad shows the floor it takes you to.

On the [b]minimap[/b], [b]footprints[/b] show where you've walked in the last 10 minutes or 100 m, so you can see which way you came. On the world map outside, nothing of the Hollow Halls shows in the corner of the world they're carved in.

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close Enshrouded.
[*]Open the game folder (Steam: right-click Enshrouded > Manage > Browse local files).
[*]Copy everything from the zip into it, keeping the folders: [b]dbgcore.dll[/b] next to [i]enshrouded.exe[/i], and the [b]greeneye\unlock-map-markers[/b] folder.
[*]Start the game and open the map (M).
[/list]

[b]Servers:[/b] nothing to install. The mod only runs on your own game.

[b]Install by hand:[/b] Vortex does not know the Greeneye Loader yet.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]greeneye\unlock-map-markers[/i]. If no other Greeneye mod is left, also delete [i]dbgcore.dll[/i] and the [i]greeneye[/i] folder.

[line]

[size=4][b]Languages[/b][/size]

The mod's text follows the game's language: English, German, French, Italian, Spanish, Portuguese (Brazil), Polish, Russian, Ukrainian, Turkish, Japanese, Korean, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese and Thai. Marker and region names come from the game itself.

To use another language, set [i]Language=[/i] in [i]greeneye\unlock-map-markers\minimap_config.ini[/i] under [i][General][/i]: [i]auto[/i] (follows the game), or [i]english, german, french, italian, spanish, brazilian, polish, russian, ukrainian, turkish, japanese, koreana, schinese, tchinese, thai[/i]. Restart the game after changing it.

[b]Graphics memory[/b]: the game keeps the world map's textures in 128 MB of graphics memory, too little for the whole map (its north was drawn dark, without sea), so the mod gives them 256 MB. On a graphics card short of memory, set [i]PotatoPC=true[/i] under [i][General][/i] in the same file to keep the game's 128 MB, and restart the game.

The translations are my own. If something reads wrong in your language, please say so in the Posts tab.

[line]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Single player, hosting your own game, and dedicated servers[/b], all with the mod on your game only.
[*][b]Plays well with other mods.[/b] It runs through the Greeneye Loader ([i]dbgcore.dll[/i], shared with Find, Quick Deposit, Continue and Embervale Teleport). Where another mod hooks the same game function, it chains onto that hook instead of replacing it.
[*]With the [b]Find[/b] mod installed, Find on the map uses Find's search box. G G uses the same glow as Find and Quick Deposit, and all three work together.
[*][b]Safe on game updates.[/b] Made for the current game version. If an update changes code the mod patches, it skips that part instead of crashing, and the log says so.
[*]Works with Steam. Not tested with other store versions.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

If something doesn't work, please post these files with your report. Both are in the game folder:
[list]
[*][i]greeneye\unlock-map-markers\unlock_map_markers.log[/i]: what the mod found and patched.
[*][i]greeneye\unlock-map-markers\unlock_map_markers.old.log[/i]: the log's earlier part, if there is one (the log rolls over at 10 MB).
[*][i]greeneye\loader.log[/i]: what the Greeneye Loader did.
[/list]
[b]Ctrl + Shift + F12[/b] switches the whole mod off and on, to compare with the game as it is (best with the world map open).

[line]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[b]1.3.50[/b]
[list]
[*]Waypoint on the minimap: your waypoint shows where it is, and at the minimap's edge, pointing its way, when it's further off. Requested by harag.
[*]Alt+Shift+M (LB + D-pad Down on a controller; OpenSettings under [Keys]) opens Settings while you play, on the World Map, and from the game's own map with Vanilla World Map on. Requested by MaZyGer.
[*]Switching Nearby Creatures Only on shows a notice with the creatures it tracks, or that none are on, with Don't show again.
[*]Dungeon maps show the dungeon's name at the top (a Hollow Hall with its region). Ctrl+D (LB + D-pad Up on a controller; DungeonMapToggle under [Keys]) switches between the dungeon's map and the overworld's, with its hint in the key bar. Requested by JudgeHellboy.
[*]In an Ancient Spire, its top, where its teleport lands you, shows the overworld on the World Map and the minimap; past its first teleporter, the spire's own map.
[*]Stacked Pins List (Settings, off by default): rest the cursor on pins on top of each other and a card lists them all; a row lights its pin and a click opens its menu.
[*]Find on the map also finds a place by its unread rumor ("hope set" finds the Sunken Ancient City) and by the quest it is shown for, and one click on a result goes there.
[*]A place with an unread rumor shows the rumor's line under its name, as on the game's own map.
[*]Roads draw closer to their real width. Requested by Maxos5000.
[*]Opened from a quest's "show on map" prompt, the World Map stays on the quest instead of centring on you, and a controller button still held from the prompt no longer opens the Map Key. Reported by True2Kozy.
[*]Esc with Settings open closes Settings and keeps the map open. The Map Key stays folded or unfolded as you left it. The cursor's position plate sits at the top, clear of the key hints.
[*]The mod's pins draw under a quest's or rumor's card (with the Map Desk) and under the level numbers.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]A Night Sanctum or other place inside a quest's search circle disappeared under the quest's pin: it keeps its own icon. Reported by Ykses.
[*]With Facing Up, the minimap in a vault or Hollow Hall stopped turning or turned round the wrong spot. Reported by Ykses.
[*]The Sunken Ancient City showed as Follow The Melody, or as an empty diamond: it shows under its own name, follows the Ancient Vault row and is found by Find.
[*]A dungeon's map had none of the mod's key hints, and the dungeon's map covered the game's upper row of hints.
[*]With Vanilla World Map on and the minimap's info bar off, nothing on a keyboard opened Settings. Reported by MaZyGer.
[*]A Gold Chest inside a quest's search circle showed plain text instead of its name panel.
[/list]

[b]1.3.49[/b]
[list]
[*]Minimap Rotation (Settings > Minimap): Facing Up turns the minimap with your character, so the way you face is always up and the N shows where north is. North Up keeps it as before.
[*]Find on the map matches like Find's own search: words in any order ("chest gold" finds the Gold Chests), then names with only some of the words. Enter with nothing selected shows only the best matches. Exact match (Ctrl+E or the controller's Y; FindExactMatch under [Keys]) keeps only names holding the whole text; with a newer Find it is also a checkbox in the box.
[*]Click one of the mod's own icons (a collectible, a lore note, an ore, a Wooden Chest, a Town Portal) for the game's Send Ping and Set as Waypoint. A rumor's "?" the game keeps hidden shows its name and opens its menu with Go to Journal.
[*]F on a Journal entry turns its Map Key row back on when it was off, so what you asked to see shows.
[*]Quests another player finished but you haven't (the Journal's Missed list) show again under Main Quest or Side Quest.
[*]Roads are read from the finer terrain, so a road under a little dirt or moss shows, and on the Map Desk they draw under every pin and menu.
[*]Map Desk: drag the map out over the desk; let go and it floats back until the map's edge is mid-screen, so a place at the world's edge can be brought to the middle.
[*]Press on a pin and drag, and the map pans, on a crowded map too; letting go doesn't open the pin's menu.
[*]Hover names always draw over the pins and never over an open marker menu, and a quest pin's name shows on the same dark panel. An icon inside a quest's search circle keeps its own name.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]With Looted / Read / Beaten on Grayed Out, beaten bosses were so faint they looked gone: they now keep a gray ring, their size and the check mark. Reported by izisot.
[*]Gold and Silver Chest pins offered Remove Marker.
[*]Clicking an icon inside a quest's search circle opened the quest's menu.
[/list]

[b]1.3.48[/b]
[list]
[*]Map Desk: the World Map now lies on a painted cartographer's desk that pans and zooms with it, with a gold frame, a lantern with a soft blue glow, a 3D compass that holds north and swings when you drag the map, and two survivor notes written in the game's language. With it on, panning stops at the map's edges at every zoom. Settings > Look > Map Desk turns it off; it starts on only with the game's Ultra graphics preset.
[*]Mark places done: Ctrl + click a town, camp, sanctum, vault or other place to give it a check mark, and again to clear it. Marked places follow Completed Places: Hide, and Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y undo and redo marks too. A visited sanctum's check mark can be cleared the same way. Elixir Wells and Roots are left to the game.
[*]Nearby Creatures Only (Settings > Minimap): the minimap shows the live creatures within 75 m instead of their spawn points, with height arrows and a ring while an enemy fights you (red) or searches for you (amber), and G G outlines them through walls. Hide on World Map, under it, keeps their spawn points off the World Map too, except the creatures Find is looking for. Requested by cutegirl16owo.
[*]Hover names on the World Map show on a dark panel so they read on a crowded map. The hover name, Alt + click and Ctrl + click all follow the marker the game itself highlights.
[*]A place with both a quest and an unread rumor now shows the quest's name when you hover it: the Sunken Ancient City shows Follow The Melody.
[*]Settings are grouped under World Map, Minimap, Look and Filters. New in Look: Dungeon Maps turns the Hollow Hall, vault and spire maps off, and the map then opens on the hall's entrance. Requested by izisot.
[*]Filter presets can be saved from the keyboard with Ctrl+Alt+1 to Ctrl+Alt+5 (SavePreset1 to SavePreset5 under [Keys]), and the preset keys no longer also reach the game. Requested by Ykses.
[*]Nothing around you is hidden any more: the mod's icons and check marks draw under your arrow and its ring, the key hints and the legend instead of being left out. Creature and resource pins fill in nearest you first when there are more than the map draws at once.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Alt + click on an Ancient Spire could hide a nearby ore or chest row instead.
[*]Alt + click didn't hide a lore rumor's "?" pin.
[*]Ctrl + click on a quest pin marked the place under it done.
[*]Long names in the Map Key ran under the padlock and ON / OFF, and the presets' tip ran out of its box.
[/list]

[b]1.3.47[/b]
[list]
[*]Roads and Surface Water, two new rows under GROUND in the Map Key, on the World Map and the minimap. Roads draws every road on the island (dirt, stone, limestone and the Kindlewastes' ancient roads) from the game's own world files; Surface Water draws its lakes, rivers and pools as the world starts out (water you build or drain isn't shown).
[*]They're drawn finer the closer you zoom in, and kept in presets like the other rows.
[/list]

[b]1.3.46[/b]
[list]
[*]Filter presets: five slots under Show All / Hide All in the Map Key. Click one to apply it, Ctrl + click to save your current filters into it, right click to give it your own name. A preset also keeps the map settings: fog and pins (Explored / Hybrid / Reveal All), marker size, looted and completed places, the region filter, region names and level areas.
[*]Alt+1 to Alt+5 apply a preset from the World Map; on a controller LT + Left/Right steps through them. They start as Chests, Mining, Exploring, Bosses and Plants, each keeping other players, town portals, custom pins and the main quest on.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Inside a Hollow Hall, Pins: Explored hid the hall's chests and notes (Hybrid grayed them), even ones already found: the game's fog never clears in the halls' corner. The hall you're in now counts as explored (reported by Ykses).
[*]A new world could take over an old world's looted chests when its first Flame Altar stood where one of the old world's did. A world is now recognised by most of its altars, not one (reported by FWSWBN).
[/list]

[b]1.3.45[/b]
[list]
[*]Ancient Vaults and Ancient Spires get dungeon maps like the Hollow Halls: the World Map and minimap show the floor you're on, with its walls, teleport pads, exits, chests and lore notes. Teleporters split a vault or spire into floors: - Floor n / m + on the map picks one (Ctrl+Up/Down, or LT+Up/Down on a controller), and the map opens on the floor you stand on.
[*]Their traps are drawn live: fireballs and spark beams move on the map in time with the game, spike plates glow red as their spikes come out, and plates turned off by their switch show as off. Doors show whether they're locked, closed or open, and barred windows that can't be broken show as walls. Hover a teleport pad to see which floor it takes you to, up or down.
[*]On the dungeon maps the player arrow points the way your character faces, not the camera, and is a dotted outline when you're on another floor than the one shown. Footprints now look like left and right feet, so you can see which way you walked.
[*]Find on the map is off on a dungeon's own map; Shift+F still searches the skill tree.
[*]Bosses: the Heavy Ancient Construct's four spots are marked, and a killed boss now counts only for its own spot, so spots close together (such as Engine Chambers' S.P.D.R. Construct above a camp) track their kills separately.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Inside a vault or spire the minimap showed a fast travel icon.
[*]G G could light a bowl beside a lore note instead of the note.
[*]A chest's height arrow on the minimap flickered when the chest was near the height where the arrow shows.
[/list]

[b]1.3.44[/b]
[list]
[*]With Completed Places on Hide, a completed place you've put a waypoint on stays on the map, so you can click it to clear the waypoint.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]A waypoint on a read obelisk or another completed place couldn't be cleared while Completed Places was on Hide: only an empty diamond showed.
[*]Chest outlines (G twice) also lit things standing at a chest or lore note, such as the scaffold under a chest, and drew a large flat shape around it. Only the chest or note lights up now.
[/list]

[b]1.3.43[/b]
[list]
[*]Each Hollow Halls chest now belongs to one hall, so a hall's World Map and minimap no longer show chests from a neighbouring hall. Seven gold and silver chests on ledges and in secret rooms now show on their own hall's map.
[*]On the overworld, wooden chests and resource icons now thin out only as you zoom, no longer as you pan.
[*]With Town Portals 1.0.13, players show on the minimap in the colour they picked with its PortalColor setting.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Chests from other Hollow Halls showed on a hall's map (reported by Lomack02).
[*]Some chests on a hall's map appeared and disappeared as you panned. Hall maps now draw every chest.
[/list]

[b]1.3.42[/b]
[list]
[*]Controller on the World Map: RS + D-pad Up marks what is at the middle of the view looted, read or beaten, like Ctrl + click. RS + D-pad Down hides its row, like Alt + click. RS + D-pad Left and Right undo and redo filter changes. RS is pressing the right stick in; the left stick moves the view. MarkChestPad, HideRowPad, FilterUndo and FilterRedo under [Keys] rebind them.
[*]Fixed: a World Map opened from the controller's menu showed none of the mod's tips at the bottom.
[*]With Embervale Teleport installed, the map's tips show its Teleport button, and follow a rebind.
[*]Should fix the Map Key missing controller presses at high frame rates. Reported by Ykses.
[/list]

[b]1.3.41[/b]
[list]
[*]New Plants rows, so the map and its Find box can find them: Date (palms showing fruit) and Yucca Fruit, in every language.
[*]The Find box's list can be hovered and clicked again, and Tab no longer types a space. This came from Find 1.2.9: update Find to 1.2.10 as well.
[/list]

